gallery:["photo-1519741497674-611481863552","photo-1519167758481-83f550bb49b3","photo-1492684223066-81342ee5ff30"],
sections:[
{title:"Wedding celebrations",body:"Explore the atmosphere and logistics of wedding events, from ceremony requirements and guest experience to décor, vendor coordination and schedules."},
{title:"Traditional ceremony settings",body:"Different ceremonies bring distinct sequences, family needs and cultural expectations. The course discusses respectful planning across traditions."},
{title:"Nikah and reception settings",body:"Study how ceremony timing, guest movement, venue coordination and family communication can shape the planning of a Nikah and its accompanying celebration."},
{title:"Christian weddings",body:"Explore ceremony and reception formats, programme sequence, venue details and supplier coordination in a Christian wedding context."},
{title:"Engagement and pre-wedding events",body:"Smaller pre-wedding functions demonstrate how event concepts, décor, invitations, guest lists and timelines can be planned for a focused celebration."},
{title:"Birthday and private parties",body:"Private events highlight the importance of personal preferences, entertainment, guest experience and a clear schedule."},
{title:"Corporate conferences",body:"Corporate event environments bring together programme planning, venue flow, delegate needs, speakers, stage production and professional communication."},
{title:"Product launches",body:"Launch events can require message discipline, presentation timing, brand visibility, media coordination and a carefully planned guest journey."},
{title:"Brand promotions",body:"Promotional events show how event design, audience interaction and marketing objectives need to work together."},
{title:"Stage shows and concerts",body:"Live performances involve stage transitions, backstage coordination, technical requirements and communication across production teams."},
{title:"Cultural programmes",body:"Cultural and traditional performances require attention to programme sequencing, performer requirements, timing and audience movement."},
{title:"Exhibitions and trade fairs",body:"Exhibitions introduce booth layouts, exhibitor coordination, signage, visitor movement and the management of shared event spaces."},
{title:"Destination and luxury events",body:"Destination and luxury formats can involve layered supplier coordination, travel logistics, guest communication and detailed contingency planning."},
{title:"Festivals and community events",body:"Community and festival environments can involve public access, schedules, safety considerations, vendors and multi-activity coordination."},
{title:"Décor and stage styling",body:"Décor and stage design connect the event concept with venue constraints, materials, installation time, production and budget."},
{title:"Behind-the-scenes operations",body:"The visible event is supported by preparation, supplier arrivals, checklists, setup schedules, coordination and event-day problem-solving."},
{title:"Classroom and practical learning",body:"The institute’s training environment includes classroom lessons, project discussions, mock client meetings and practical demonstrations."},
{title:"A note about image authenticity",body:"Replace illustrative images with Anugraha’s own approved event photographs as they become available. Captions must identify the real event and must not imply ownership of third-party work."}
],
closingTitle:"The next gallery update should show Anugraha’s real work.",
closingText:"Approved event photographs and student-created work can replace these illustrative images over time."
