admissions: {
tag:"ADMISSIONS",
title:"A clear process, before you make a decision.",
subtitle:"Start with counselling. Understand the programme. Then decide.",
intro:"Anugraha’s admission journey begins with a counselling request and a conversation with the founders. Prospective learners can visit the centre, review the curriculum, discuss career interests and understand fee and payment details before confirming a place.",
photo:"photo-1523580494863-6f3031224c94",
gallery:["photo-1524178232363-1fb2b075b655","photo-1521737711867-e3b97375f902","photo-1497366754035-f200968a6e72"],
sections:[
{title:"Admission overview",body:"The admission journey is designed to help each applicant understand the course and decide whether it matches their goals before making a payment."},
{title:"Who can apply",body:"The programme is open to students, graduates, working professionals, homemakers, freelancers, career changers and aspiring entrepreneurs."},
{title:"Minimum age",body:"Applicants must be at least 16 years old. Anyone below 18 must have parent or guardian consent."},
{title:"No minimum qualification",body:"There is no minimum educational qualification requirement. Counselling helps the team understand each learner’s background and interest."},
{title:"Step 1 · Send a counselling request",body:"Share your name, phone number and basic learning interests through the enquiry form or contact the admissions team directly."},
{title:"Step 2 · Admissions team follow-up",body:"The team reviews the enquiry and contacts the applicant to understand their questions and arrange a counselling conversation."},
{title:"Step 3 · Meet the founders",body:"The founders explain the 45-day programme, teaching approach, observational exposure and the practical activities included."},
{title:"Step 4 · Visit the Vijayanagar centre",body:"Prospective learners can visit the centre, see the classroom and facilities, and understand where offline learning takes place."},
{title:"Step 5 · Review the curriculum",body:"Discuss the topics covered, practical assignments, event formats, vendor sourcing, budgeting, client handling and final assessment."},
{title:"Step 6 · Discuss your goals",body:"Talk about your education, current occupation, interests and whether you are exploring employment, freelancing, entrepreneurship or general skill development."},
{title:"Step 7 · Understand industry exposure",body:"The team explains the 10–15 days of observational exposure, how visits are arranged and why specific event formats depend on schedules and access."},
{title:"Step 8 · Review fee and payment details",body:"The admissions team shares the current course fee and payment instructions during counselling. The public website does not publish a fee until the institute confirms it."},
{title:"Step 9 · Confirm admission",body:"Once the learner decides to proceed, the team confirms the admission requirements and records the payment and admission details."},
{title:"Payment and receipt",body:"The current process is full payment at admission. Learners should keep the payment confirmation and receipt supplied by the institute."},
{title:"Batch size and intake cycle",body:"The planned batch size is 20–25 learners and a new batch cycle is planned every 45 days. The team confirms actual availability and start dates."},
{title:"Course communication",body:"After admission, schedules, announcements and learning resources are shared through WhatsApp and Google Drive. There is no separate student login portal at present."},
{title:"Attendance and practical progress",body:"The institute communicates course schedules, assignments and progress updates. Students are expected to participate in classroom and practical learning activities."},
{title:"Certificates and completion",body:"Anugraha issues its own course completion certificate and a separate practical experience certificate, subject to completion requirements. External accreditation is not confirmed."},
{title:"What to ask before you enrol",body:"Ask about batch dates, course fee, timetable, language availability, observational visit expectations, certificate details and any personal support you may need."}
],
closingTitle:"The next step is a conversation.",
closingText:"Call 96865 68245 or request counselling to understand the current intake."
},
